{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a2a41815",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Paired Z-memory benchmark analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook reads explicitly selected saved runs. It performs no simulation or decoding.\n",
    "Figures and statistics come from the reusable `analysis` package. Run/scientific/decoder/\n",
    "execution groups remain separate. BB uses one block trial per shot with all 12 observables.\n",
    "Smoke plots validate software and do not establish decoder superiority."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "790b50ba",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import os\n",
    "# The execution CLI supplies CONFIG_PATH/RUN_PATHS. Interactive users can set these\n",
    "# variables first, or set QEC_ANALYSIS_CONFIG and QEC_ANALYSIS_RUN.\n",
    "ROOT = next((p for p in (Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents) if (p / \"pyproject.toml\").is_file()), Path.cwd())\n",
    "CONFIG_PATH = globals().get(\"CONFIG_PATH\", os.environ.get(\"QEC_ANALYSIS_CONFIG\", str(ROOT / \"config/smoke.yaml\")))\n",
    "RUN_PATHS = globals().get(\"RUN_PATHS\", [os.environ[\"QEC_ANALYSIS_RUN\"]] if \"QEC_ANALYSIS_RUN\" in os.environ else [])\n",
    "if not RUN_PATHS:\n",
    "    raise ValueError(\"Select saved run paths explicitly in RUN_PATHS or QEC_ANALYSIS_RUN\")\n",
    "from qec_bp_benchmark.config import load_config\n",
    "from qec_bp_benchmark.runner import configure_execution\n",
    "config = load_config(CONFIG_PATH)\n",
    "configure_execution(config)\n",
    "import matplotlib\n",
    "matplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\n",
    "from analysis import load_run, create_report\n",
    "runs = [load_run(path) for path in RUN_PATHS]\n",
    "[(run.manifest[\"run_id\"], run.manifest[\"status\"], run.samples.num_rows, run.decodes.num_rows) for run in runs]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0ceb9358",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Export validated summaries and figures\n",
    "\n",
    "Block failure = decoding failure OR any valid logical mismatch. Component rates use all\n",
    "shots; conditional mismatch uses valid outputs. Wilson intervals count physical shots,\n",
    "not BB observable bits. Zero-event triangles show the two-sided Wilson upper endpoint,\n",
    "not a positive estimated rate. Timings are complete-block CPU/wall durations; no division\n",
    "by extraction rounds is performed. Tail tables retain sample size and N(1-q)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e8d5da1f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "report = create_report(RUN_PATHS, config.analysis.output, settings=config.analysis)\n",
    "print(report)\n",
    "import json\n",
    "failures = json.loads((report / \"failures.json\").read_text())[\"groups\"]\n",
    "[(r[\"family\"], r[\"distance\"], r[\"decoder_name\"], r[\"shots\"], r[\"block_failure\"]) for r in failures]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "fc1b7990",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "timings = json.loads((report / \"timings.json\").read_text())[\"groups\"]\n",
    "[(r[\"family\"], r[\"distance\"], r[\"decoder_name\"], r[\"timing_mode\"], r[\"timer\"],\n",
    "  r[\"samples\"], r[\"mean_ns\"], r[\"p99_ns\"], r[\"quantiles\"][-1]) for r in timings]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8e215027",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from IPython.display import Image, display\n",
    "for figure in sorted((report / \"figures\").glob(\"*.png\")):\n",
    "    display(Image(filename=str(figure)))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5337509e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The exported JSON keeps complete grouping keys, denominators, method/profile identities,\n",
    "confidence levels, quantile method and low-tail flags. PNG/PDF files are standalone artifacts.\n",
    "The report manifest records source-run manifest hashes and output checksums. This notebook\n",
    "contains selection/display calls only; statistical and plotting implementations live in `analysis/`."
   ]
  }
 ],
